  Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0.

  android:allowBackup="false" opts out of cloud backup and restore, but it does
  not govern the Android 12+ device-to-device transfer path, and the platform
  documentation warns that on devices from some manufacturers app files cannot
  be kept out of D2D migration at all. This file is the documented control for
  that path, so the wallet tree (the chain database plus the encrypted vault
  under filesDir) is excluded from it explicitly.

  Every domain is listed rather than relying on "root" alone: the domains are
  separate extraction trees, so an exclusion of one does not cover the others.

  cloud-backup repeats the exclusions even though allowBackup="false" already
  disables that path, so flipping allowBackup can never silently re-enrol the
  wallet in a cloud backup.

  Ignored on Android 11 and lower, which have no D2D transfer path and where
  allowBackup="false" is the whole opt-out.
-->
<data-extraction-rules>
    <cloud-backup>
        <exclude domain="root" />
        <exclude domain="file" />
        <exclude domain="database" />
        <exclude domain="sharedpref" />
        <exclude domain="external" />
    </cloud-backup>
    <device-transfer>
        <exclude domain="root" />
        <exclude domain="file" />
        <exclude domain="database" />
        <exclude domain="sharedpref" />
        <exclude domain="external" />
    </device-transfer>
</data-extraction-rules>
